{"name":"Vintage","hex":"#847592","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vintage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The yield of grapes or wine from a vineyard or district during one season.","Wine, especially high-quality, identified as to year and vineyard or district of origin."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to a vintage, or to wine identified by a specific vintage.","Having an enduring appeal; high-quality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vintage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vintage","blocks":[{"text":"In winemaking, vintage is the process of picking grapes to create wine. A vintage wine is one made from grapes that were all, or primarily, grown and harvested in a single specified year. In certain wines, it can denote quality, as in Port wine, where Port houses make and declare vintage Port in their best years. From this tradition, a common, though not strictly correct, usage applies the term to any wine that is perceived to be particularly old or of a particularly high quality."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cup_vintage_Cdm_Paris_320_n1.jpg/330px-Cup_vintage_Cdm_Paris_320_n1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vintage","wikidata":"Q1975981"},{"title":"Vintage (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Vintage is a Russian pop group formed in 2006 by the singer Anna Pletnyova and musician Alexey Romanof."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/%D0%9F%D0%BB%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%BD%D1%91%D0%B2%D0%B0_%D0%A0%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B2_%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BD%D1%86%D0%B5%D1%80%D1%82_%D0%B2_%D0%9A%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BA%D1%83%D1%81%D0%B5.jpg/330px-%D0%9F%D0%BB%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%BD%D1%91%D0%B2%D0%B0_%D0%A0%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B2_%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BD%D1%86%D0%B5%D1%80%D1%82_%D0%B2_%D0%9A%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BA%D1%83%D1%81%D0%B5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_conten